  "worked_solution": "We start by integrating the velocity to get $x(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & =\\int v(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\int -7\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =-7t+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo determine $C$, we use the fact that $x(4)=30.$ Substituting this into the above gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}30 & =-7(4)+C \\\\ 30 & =-28+C \\\\ C & =58.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the position $x$ of the particle at time $t$ is \n\n$$\nx(t)=-7t+58.\n$$",
